=============================================================================
1. Model weights derived from third-party pre-trained models
=============================================================================

The trained weights are not stored in this repository. They are published as
release assets and restored by scripts/download_models.py. Two of the models are
derived from pre-trained weights released under a non-commercial licence, and
that restriction carries over to the derived weights. This is one of the two
reasons the whole of FlatMorphAI is distributed non-commercially.

1.1 Segmentation model -- derived from Mask2Former

  Folders:   checkpoints_segmentation_model/
             mask2former-swin-tiny-ade-semantic/
             flatmorphai/regen_stage_v20/models/mask2former_segmentation/

  Original:  Mask2Former, "Masked-attention Mask Transformer for Universal
             Image Segmentation", B. Cheng, I. Misra, A. G. Schwing,
             A. Kirillov, R. Girdhar, CVPR 2022, arXiv:2112.01527.
             Checkpoint facebook/mask2former-swin-tiny-ade-semantic,
             Meta AI (Facebook AI Research).
             https://github.com/facebookresearch/Mask2Former
             https://huggingface.co/facebook/mask2former-swin-tiny-ade-semantic

  Terms:     The Mask2Former model zoo states: "All models available for
             download through this document are licensed under the Creative
             Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International License."
             https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
             The Mask2Former SOURCE CODE is under the MIT licence; it is
             distinct from the weights and is not redistributed here (the
             model is run through the Hugging Face transformers package).

  CHANGES:   mask2former-swin-tiny-ade-semantic/ is the original checkpoint.
             checkpoints_segmentation_model/ and the copy used by the
             regeneration chain were MODIFIED: fine-tuned on planarian images
             to segment the worm.

1.2 Regeneration state classifier -- derived from ConvNeXt V2

  Folder:    flatmorphai/regen_stage_v20/models/stage_classifier/

  Original:  ConvNeXt V2, "ConvNeXt V2: Co-designing and Scaling ConvNets with
             Masked Autoencoders", S. Woo, S. Debnath, R. Hu, X. Chen, Z. Liu,
             I. S. Kweon, S. Xie, CVPR 2023, arXiv:2301.00808.
             Backbone convnextv2_base.fcmae_ft_in22k_in1k_384, Meta AI,
             obtained through the timm package.
             https://github.com/facebookresearch/ConvNeXt-V2

  Terms:     The ConvNeXt V2 project states that it is "released under the MIT
             license except ImageNet pre-trained and fine-tuned models which
             are licensed under a CC-BY-NC."

  CHANGES:   MODIFIED: the backbone was fine-tuned, inside a two-branch model
             (image branch and descriptor branch), to predict the regeneration
             state of planarian heads.

1.3 U-Net encoders

  Folders:   flatmorphai/regen_stage_v20/models/ (blastema and eye U-Nets)

  Original:  U-Nets built with segmentation_models_pytorch (MIT licence,
             https://github.com/qubvel-org/segmentation_models.pytorch) on a
             timm-efficientnet-b0 encoder initialised from ImageNet
             pre-trained weights distributed through that package. Those
             weights originate from the EfficientNet releases of Google
             Research and their PyTorch ports; consult the upstream release
             for their exact terms.

  CHANGES:   MODIFIED: the whole networks were trained on planarian images
             (blastema segmentation, eye detection).

1.4 Stereotype classifier

  Folder:    lightgbm_stereotype_classifier/models/

  LightGBM gradient-boosted trees trained from scratch on descriptors computed
  for this project. No third-party pre-trained weights. LightGBM itself
  (MIT licence, https://github.com/microsoft/LightGBM) is installed as a
  dependency and not redistributed.


